{"id": 39, "ts": 1783811314.845188, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "agent_1", "message": "I remain inclined to recommend **Candidate\u202fC** as the best overall fit. As Markus and Sofia highlighted, C\u2019s ability to anticipate dangerous situations, see complex connections, and his excellent spatial vision directly support the critical decision\u2011quality and technical\u2011competence criteria for long\u2011distance flights. While I acknowledge the concerns about his openness to criticism and occasional disorganization, these issues have not yet been shown to outweigh his strong leadership and situational awareness.\nIn contrast, Candidate\u202fA, though 100\u202f% reliable and able to create a positive crew atmosphere, struggles with communication and shows little willingness to continue education\u2014both important for ongoing CRM and adaptability. Candidate\u202fB\u2019s conscientiousness and stress handling are promising, but his grumpiness and uncooperative attitude raise red flags for crew cooperation, and we still lack evidence of his safety\u2011critical decision making. Candidate\u202fD, despite solid problem\u2011solving and responsibility, is described as arrogant with weak leadership, and we have no data on his professional communication or crew\u2011cooperation.\nGiven the current evidence, C\u2019s technical and leadership strengths remain the most compelling for the safety\u2011critical role, provided we can address his feedback\u2011orientation through targeted development. I therefore keep my provisional vote for **Candidate\u202fC**."}
